{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"0caae3c568fa58d165706c89a02779db8f71bcb3c8d964515eb19f01645a605c","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_ecfb84b8aff60065fbedd0a7286f65d7ccce252a810d65e9cd26294d933325ac","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical method for generating labeled data for a specific computer vision task involving honeybees. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific privacy, anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact policies, as the paper does not contain explicit statements regarding these areas.","paper_id":"BkGakb9lx","paper_identity_sha256":"79cef3b278f3de9a6796eabac488bf7476184cb7790b58ea9f0e18958c620c75","prompt_identity_sha256":"2be8eaea7506027a6423bb23b1597bba23edc455a38f2f6e3660b790b152ee56","raw_response_sha256":"6b385113b2f188435c8a2841fb61a498df1b98d65f02f7fdce1b1d5b535e37aa","request_identity_sha256":"dc3bedc1cca4ad4fe7be1a57fce23e752c7b8e442231f004c74d9ef5bd0a731f","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"fc11181cf72a8673ed59576266ee8d9d2d498001cf631dc0ed7722506f624e8d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-013"],"review_text":"The paper describes the use of a framework to generate data for tracking honeybees in the BeesBook project. The application involves identifying individual bees via tags to analyze social behavior. The text does not discuss potential ethical risks, such as the welfare of the bees, the impact of tagging on their behavior, or broader societal harms. No specific ethical considerations or mitigation strategies are provided in the visible text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-013","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes 2.4 million unlabeled images and 66,000 labeled tags from the BeesBook project. The data consists of images of honeybees with attached tags. The text does not mention data licensing, consent, or privacy regulations. Since the data involves animals rather than humans, standard human privacy regulations may not apply, but the paper does not specify the source of the data or any agreements regarding its use. The evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific data usage policies.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper lists the authors as Leon Sixt, Benjamin Wild, and Tim Landgraf, along with their affiliation at Freie Universität Berlin and email addresses. The metadata indicates the venue is ICLR 2017. Without a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for this specific submission context, it is not possible to declare a violation or clearance. The visible names and affiliations are present in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work, but there is no auditable evidence of textual overlap or simultaneous submission to other venues. The absence of evidence does not prove originality or the absence of misconduct.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a checklist, or explicit mentions of IRB/ethics approvals. It does not specify software or data licenses. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for this venue and year, the absence of these elements cannot be judged as a compliance failure. The evidence is insufficient to determine policy compliance regarding broader impact documentation.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"3b4ab740587045c87bc8a501dd5e9be3f73f132b15bfd4fa5ffa105eb056d885","paper_id":"BkGakb9lx","paper_ordinal":47,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha